---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL } from "../lib/site";
const sections = [["scope", "Scope"], ["reporting", "Security reports"], ["responsibilities", "Protect your environment"]] as const;
---
<LegalPage title="Security information — Weavra" description="Security information for the Weavra development project." heading="Security information" lede="Secure the environments you operate and review the source applicable to your build." sections={sections}>
  <section id="scope">
    <p class="section-number">01</p><h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>Weavra is in development. This distribution does not operate an inherited account or relay service. The original T3 Tools security policy and contacts do not describe a Weavra-operated service.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="reporting">
    <p class="section-number">02</p><h2>Security reports</h2>
    <p>Consult the <a href={GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}>source repository</a> for current maintainer information and any published reporting instructions. A dedicated private reporting channel, response-time commitment, bounty or legal safe harbor is not established by this page.</p>
    <p>Do not publish credentials, personal data or sensitive exploit details in a public issue. Revoke exposed credentials before sharing sanitized evidence.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="responsibilities">
    <p class="section-number">03</p><h2>Protect your environment</h2>
    <p>Test only systems you own or are authorized to assess. Protect connection credentials and local state, keep backups, review provider permissions, and inspect commands and source changes before executing them.</p>
    <p>Product updates are not automatically supplied by this development distribution. Review repository changes and your selected providers' guidance when maintaining your installation.</p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
